cla_mmrs, dst_mmrs: state the SMC timestamp tie-off, edge-select range and W2C self-clear

Three descriptions read for the generic block and hid SMC behaviour:
- trDstTimestampConfig source 0 is the external timestamp input, which the
  SMC ties to zero, so at reset every DST timestamp packet carries zero.
- Signal0Select and Signal1Select are 7 bits, but only indices below the
  debug signal width (64 in the SMC) select a signal.
- Each CDbgEapStatus W2C bit is cleared by hardware one cycle after it
  rises, so a further clear needs another write of 1.

Recorded as a patch so the hand-mirrored upstream/ tree stays
reproducible from the vendored spec plus patches/ applied in order.
